        "text": "The primary outcomes included the development of preeclampsia, early-onset preeclampsia, late-onset preeclampsia, and gestational hypertension, as well as the delivery of an SGA neonate from patients without preeclampsia. Gestational hypertension was included in the outcomes due to its association with adverse pregnancy outcomes 44 and the possibility that this pregnancy complication may represent an intermediate phenotype in the spectrum of antiangiogenic states that include preeclampsia and SGA. 45,46 Secondary outcomes were placental abruption and a composite of severe neonatal morbidities that included intraventricular hemorrhage, necrotizing enterocolitis, and hyaline membrane disease with postnatal sonographic/radiologic confirmation.",
        "snippetKind": "body",
